    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test \u2014 the sole test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature for `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}`. The request may include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner response now exposes a derived `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (DTO source of truth):\n   - Added writable `title` string field to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n   - Added read-only derived `salutation` string field to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `title` column with getter/setter so the title survives the create\u2192reload round-trip.\n\n3. **`mapper/Salutation.java`** (new) \u2014 the derivation helper, matching the existing `ContactPreference`/`AgeBand` style.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 maps `salutation` via `Salutation.of(owner)`; `title` maps through automatically by name (String\u2194String) in both directions.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses hsqldb; the others were kept consistent.\n\nNo new function classes or YAML were needed \u2014 `title` flows through the existing `ValidateOwner \u2192 BuildOwner \u2192 \u2026 \u2192 RespondWith*` pipeline as an ordinary owner field, and `salutation` is a mapper-derived read field like the other computed fields (`displayName`, `initials`, etc.).",
